WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.548 --> 00:00:02.330
- Second game we're
playing against Air Force.

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:04.195
Got late in the game, fourth quarter.

00:00:04.195 --> 00:00:06.208
Guy dropped back he threw
the ball to a receiver

00:00:06.208 --> 00:00:07.551
coming out of my sideline.

00:00:07.551 --> 00:00:09.076
Me and the guy, we went head on.

00:00:09.076 --> 00:00:11.201
Soon as I hit the guy,
felt as if every breath

00:00:11.201 --> 00:00:12.464
of my body left.

00:00:12.464 --> 00:00:13.548
People think commitment is saying,

00:00:13.548 --> 00:00:16.233
"Yes, I'll do it on the
days when it feel good."

00:00:16.233 --> 00:00:17.518
But I have been committed to everything

00:00:17.518 --> 00:00:18.870
that I ever started in my life.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.191
I never stopped and I never quitted.

00:00:21.191 --> 00:00:23.421
I don't believe in excuses.

00:00:23.421 --> 00:00:25.143
Because the thing about
if you make an excuse,

00:00:25.143 --> 00:00:27.000
the thing you have to realize about life,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.000
somebody has it ten times worse than you

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.087
and you make an excuse
because you're soft, man.

00:00:32.087 --> 00:00:34.161
- In a football game in 2006,

00:00:34.161 --> 00:00:36.120
he made a tackle that completely changed

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.607
the course of his life.

00:00:37.607 --> 00:00:39.363
He suffered a life-threatening injury

00:00:39.363 --> 00:00:40.984
that paralyzed his right arm.

00:00:40.984 --> 00:00:42.862
It turned him into a motivational speaker

00:00:42.862 --> 00:00:46.211
that encourages people to
embrace the challenges of life.

00:00:46.211 --> 00:00:48.166
He's Inky Johnson and here's my take

00:00:48.166 --> 00:00:50.172
on his top ten rules of success.

00:00:50.172 --> 00:00:51.861
Rule number one is my personal favorite

00:00:51.861 --> 00:00:53.176
and I'm super curious to figure out

00:00:53.176 --> 00:00:54.860
which one you guys like the best.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:56.161
Also, as you're watching the clips,

00:00:56.161 --> 00:00:58.392
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:58.392 --> 00:01:00.069
please leave it down in the comments below

00:01:00.069 --> 00:01:03.314
and put quotes around it so
other can be inspired as well.

00:01:03.314 --> 00:01:04.547
When you write something down,

00:01:04.547 --> 00:01:07.928
it's much more likely
to stick with you, too.

00:01:07.928 --> 00:01:08.761
Enjoy.

00:01:21.928 --> 00:01:23.864
- You know why people quit?

00:01:23.864 --> 00:01:26.459
People don't have pride in what they do.

00:01:26.459 --> 00:01:28.425
You know why people stop?

00:01:28.425 --> 00:01:31.087
They're selfish and it's just about them.

00:01:31.087 --> 00:01:32.214
When you have a bigger purpose

00:01:32.214 --> 00:01:33.532
to why you're doing what you're doing

00:01:33.532 --> 00:01:34.937
and you want to honor sacrifices

00:01:34.937 --> 00:01:36.532
that others have made for you,

00:01:36.532 --> 00:01:39.341
it's nothing for you to keep
going when you hit adversity.

00:01:39.341 --> 00:01:42.231
If every decision and choice
you make is just about you,

00:01:42.231 --> 00:01:43.740
at a certain point you
going to hit something

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:44.963
that's a lot tougher than you

00:01:44.963 --> 00:01:45.830
and it's going to make you quit

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:47.183
because you don't have a driving force

00:01:47.183 --> 00:01:48.998
for why you do what you do.

00:01:48.998 --> 00:01:50.731
But when I got up to the
University of Tennessee,

00:01:50.731 --> 00:01:51.909
it was simple.

00:01:51.909 --> 00:01:54.592
It was simple for me to
give everything I had.

00:01:54.592 --> 00:01:56.099
My freshman year I played special teams.

00:01:56.099 --> 00:01:58.191
My sophomore season I
broke the starting lineup,

00:01:58.191 --> 00:01:59.707
had a really strong sophomore season.

00:01:59.707 --> 00:02:01.076
The summer heading into my junior year,

00:02:01.076 --> 00:02:03.128
I still remember the
day where I was sitting

00:02:03.128 --> 00:02:04.977
in our film room and I was watching film

00:02:04.977 --> 00:02:06.143
on the California Bears.

00:02:06.143 --> 00:02:08.951
My defensive backs coach,
Larry Slade came in the room,

00:02:08.951 --> 00:02:11.196
he said, "Inky, I got
some good news for you."

00:02:11.196 --> 00:02:12.924
I dropped the clicker,
I said, "What is it?"

00:02:12.924 --> 00:02:15.845
He said, "Man, you're a projected
top 30 draft pick, son."

00:02:15.845 --> 00:02:16.678
He said, "All you have to do

00:02:16.678 --> 00:02:18.168
"is play the next 10 football games,

00:02:18.168 --> 00:02:20.732
"you're a automatic multi-millionaire."

00:02:20.732 --> 00:02:21.565
I went out of the room,

00:02:21.565 --> 00:02:24.139
I called my mother and my
grandmother on a three-way.

00:02:24.139 --> 00:02:27.012
I said, "After this season,
there'll be no more struggling."

00:02:27.012 --> 00:02:29.849
I said, "We will never miss another meal."

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.767
I said, "We will never
experience another Christmas

00:02:31.767 --> 00:02:33.665
"where we have to stand
on the side of the curve

00:02:33.665 --> 00:02:35.579
"and just be grateful."

00:02:35.579 --> 00:02:36.412
I hungered up.

00:02:36.412 --> 00:02:38.077
First football game, I
went out played great,

00:02:38.077 --> 00:02:39.967
got a interception, shut Cal down.

00:02:39.967 --> 00:02:41.845
Second game, we're
playing against Air Force.

00:02:41.845 --> 00:02:43.699
Got late in the game, fourth quarter.

00:02:43.699 --> 00:02:45.654
Guy dropped back he threw
the ball to a receiver

00:02:45.654 --> 00:02:47.042
coming out of my sideline.

00:02:47.042 --> 00:02:48.579
Me and the guy we went head on.

00:02:48.579 --> 00:02:50.728
Soon as I hit the guy,
felt as if every breath

00:02:50.728 --> 00:02:52.859
of my body left.

00:02:52.859 --> 00:02:55.331
Body went completely
limp, fell to the ground,

00:02:55.331 --> 00:02:56.487
I blacked out.

00:02:56.487 --> 00:02:58.443
Never happened to me before.

00:02:58.443 --> 00:02:59.764
When my eyes opened, I'll never forget,

00:02:59.764 --> 00:03:03.487
my teammates ran over they
said, "Ink get up, let's go."

00:03:03.487 --> 00:03:04.987
I said, "I can't."

00:03:05.964 --> 00:03:08.300
I said, "I can't move."

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:09.569
He said, "What do you
mean you can't move?"

00:03:09.569 --> 00:03:11.441
"You got to lock down
corner, man, we need you.

00:03:11.441 --> 00:03:12.992
"Let's go."

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:15.574
I said, "I know, man, but
this time I can't move."

00:03:15.574 --> 00:03:16.985
I flipped my head up to the sky, I said,

00:03:16.985 --> 00:03:20.085
"God, surely nothing has
happened in this moment

00:03:20.085 --> 00:03:21.813
"that can alter my life?"

00:03:21.813 --> 00:03:22.894
They got me over to the hospital,

00:03:22.894 --> 00:03:24.467
they took me back, they ran CAT scans,

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:25.710
they brought me back into my room

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.771
and, all in a 15 second time frame,

00:03:27.771 --> 00:03:29.820
the doctor came running
in from the opposite side.

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:30.997
He said, "Hey, get in here.

00:03:30.997 --> 00:03:32.603
"We got to rush this guy
back to emergency surgery,

00:03:32.603 --> 00:03:34.859
"he's about to die."

00:03:34.859 --> 00:03:36.899
I said, "What?"

00:03:36.899 --> 00:03:38.907
He said, "Son, you have
busted a subclavian artery

00:03:38.907 --> 00:03:40.249
"in your chest, you're
bleeding internally,

00:03:40.249 --> 00:03:41.393
"we have to rush you back,

00:03:41.393 --> 00:03:43.010
"take the main vein out of your left leg,

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:46.020
"plug it into your chest in
order to save your life."

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:47.330
When I opened my eyes from recovery

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:48.337
the same doctor was over me.

00:03:48.337 --> 00:03:49.791
He said, "Son, have some good news

00:03:49.791 --> 00:03:51.052
"and some bad news for you."

00:03:51.052 --> 00:03:52.423
I said, "You got some bad
news for me after telling me

00:03:52.423 --> 00:03:53.256
"I was about to die?

00:03:53.256 --> 00:03:55.882
"I'm still alive, how bad can it get?

00:03:55.882 --> 00:03:57.299
"I'm still here."

00:03:58.431 --> 00:04:00.242
He said, "The good news
is we saved your life."

00:04:00.242 --> 00:04:02.283
I said, "Thank you, sir."

00:04:02.283 --> 00:04:04.360
He said, "The bad news is,
Ink, you have nerve damage

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:05.390
"in your right shoulder."

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:07.140
I said, "Okay, cool."

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:08.899
He said, "But, son, it's
a strong possibility

00:04:08.899 --> 00:04:10.620
"that you probably can never
play the game of football

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:12.474
"again in your life."

00:04:12.474 --> 00:04:14.613
I said, "No way."

00:04:14.613 --> 00:04:16.164
I said, "No disrespect to you, Doc,

00:04:16.164 --> 00:04:18.486
"but, I've been working
for this ever since

00:04:18.486 --> 00:04:20.786
"I was seven years old."

00:04:20.786 --> 00:04:22.173
I said, "No disrespect to you, Doc,

00:04:22.173 --> 00:04:23.370
"but, you wasn't in the park with me

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:24.929
"and my mother when I was seven years old

00:04:24.929 --> 00:04:26.221
"and she was sitting in that Buick Regal

00:04:26.221 --> 00:04:27.898
"after she got done working at Wendy's.

00:04:27.898 --> 00:04:29.081
"No disrespect to you, Doc,

00:04:29.081 --> 00:04:30.871
"but you didn't come up
in that two bedroom home,

00:04:30.871 --> 00:04:32.567
"14 people sleeping on the floor.

00:04:32.567 --> 00:04:33.881
"No disrespect to you, Doc,

00:04:33.881 --> 00:04:35.696
"but you didn't miss those
meals and stay focused

00:04:35.696 --> 00:04:37.574
"and never made an excuse."

00:04:37.574 --> 00:04:38.907
I never cheated.

00:04:40.429 --> 00:04:41.762
I never cheated.

00:04:42.802 --> 00:04:44.817
Like, my conscience, still until this day,

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:47.247
won't let me, I can't cheat.

00:04:47.247 --> 00:04:49.261
I can't look myself in the mirror and say,

00:04:49.261 --> 00:04:51.391
"Ink, you did a good job,"
knowing that I cheated.

00:04:51.391 --> 00:04:52.585
I can't cheat.

00:04:52.585 --> 00:04:54.175
One of the greatest pieces of advice

00:04:54.175 --> 00:04:55.786
that my mother gave me was this,

00:04:55.786 --> 00:04:59.614
"Son, whatever you start,
you make sure you finish."

00:04:59.614 --> 00:05:00.884
And the problem with the world today,

00:05:00.884 --> 00:05:02.450
people get involved with things

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:04.352
and if they don't like a certain person,

00:05:04.352 --> 00:05:05.730
if they don't like the process,

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:08.815
if it's not what they
thought it was, they quit.

00:05:08.815 --> 00:05:10.721
And what they don't
understand about quitting,

00:05:10.721 --> 00:05:13.916
quitting becomes a habit
that doesn't just affect you.

00:05:13.916 --> 00:05:15.516
Later on in life when you get a wife

00:05:15.516 --> 00:05:17.136
and you get some kids or you get a family,

00:05:17.136 --> 00:05:18.572
it's going to come back to haunt you

00:05:18.572 --> 00:05:21.146
and it will one day affect them.

00:05:21.146 --> 00:05:22.659
That is why I tell you the process

00:05:22.659 --> 00:05:24.184
is more important than the product.

00:05:24.184 --> 00:05:26.126
It's not even about the outcome for me.

00:05:26.126 --> 00:05:28.222
It's about, can you take
pride in what you do

00:05:28.222 --> 00:05:29.055
as an individual?

00:05:29.055 --> 00:05:30.585
And every night when
you look in the mirror,

00:05:30.585 --> 00:05:33.324
knowing that you gave
everything you had to it.

00:05:33.324 --> 00:05:34.806
We have to get to the
point where we're willing

00:05:34.806 --> 00:05:38.123
to impose our will on certain things,

00:05:38.123 --> 00:05:39.743
impose your will on it.

00:05:39.743 --> 00:05:42.275
My life totally changed.

00:05:42.275 --> 00:05:45.424
And they gave me an opportunity to stop.

00:05:45.424 --> 00:05:48.097
Most people when you give
them an opportunity to stop

00:05:48.097 --> 00:05:49.317
while they're chasing something,

00:05:49.317 --> 00:05:51.497
they take advantage of it
because they feel as if,

00:05:51.497 --> 00:05:53.388
"Man, why did this have to happen to me?"

00:05:53.388 --> 00:05:55.511
I felt as if, "Why not me?"

00:05:55.511 --> 00:05:57.509
This is the perfect
opportunity to use this

00:05:57.509 --> 00:05:59.078
to be a blessing to somebody else.

00:05:59.078 --> 00:05:59.911
And you know what?

00:05:59.911 --> 00:06:01.725
It's not even about me to be truthful.

00:06:01.725 --> 00:06:02.856
It's not even about me.

00:06:02.856 --> 00:06:05.059
Now it's about we can, and
people that invested in me

00:06:05.059 --> 00:06:07.347
and saw something in me when
I couldn't see it in myself.

00:06:07.347 --> 00:06:08.439
At a certain point in life,

00:06:08.439 --> 00:06:10.128
it can't just be about you.

00:06:10.128 --> 00:06:11.509
The moment that we understand that

00:06:11.509 --> 00:06:13.440
and everyday we wake up,
we understand that life

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:14.898
is a blessing and life is a gift

00:06:14.898 --> 00:06:16.538
and if you were to check out today,

00:06:16.538 --> 00:06:18.093
how would you want to be remembered?

00:06:18.093 --> 00:06:19.843
It's bigger than you.

00:06:21.122 --> 00:06:22.068
When the bucket first started,

00:06:22.068 --> 00:06:24.396
it started over five thousand years ago.

00:06:24.396 --> 00:06:27.012
The whole purpose of a bucket list,

00:06:27.012 --> 00:06:31.289
if a guy was up on the hill
and he wanted some water

00:06:31.289 --> 00:06:33.082
and we couldn't get the guy some water

00:06:33.082 --> 00:06:35.001
or the guy couldn't get
down to get the water,

00:06:35.001 --> 00:06:36.692
we could put the water in the bucket

00:06:36.692 --> 00:06:38.477
and we can get that bucket to that guy

00:06:38.477 --> 00:06:40.898
and that water pretty
much gave that guy life.

00:06:40.898 --> 00:06:45.065
In some instances the bucket
was used to put out fires.

00:06:46.992 --> 00:06:50.009
I believe if you give everything you got

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:51.851
and everything you're a part of,

00:06:51.851 --> 00:06:53.149
like giving everything you got.

00:06:53.149 --> 00:06:54.304
It's kind of like that quote that says,

00:06:54.304 --> 00:06:56.887
"The harder you work, the
harder it is to surrender."

00:06:56.887 --> 00:06:58.563
Meaning the harder it is to give up,

00:06:58.563 --> 00:07:01.126
the harder it is to stop,
the harder it is to give in.

00:07:01.126 --> 00:07:03.194
So, if you give everything you've got

00:07:03.194 --> 00:07:05.451
to everything you're involved in,

00:07:05.451 --> 00:07:09.394
the only way you're
able to live a full life

00:07:09.394 --> 00:07:11.644
is if you empty the bucket.

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:16.736
At the end of every day
our tank should be on E

00:07:16.736 --> 00:07:20.722
and the next day our
buckets should be filled.

00:07:20.722 --> 00:07:23.394
The only way you can go back to the source

00:07:23.394 --> 00:07:24.769
is if we empty our bucket.

00:07:24.769 --> 00:07:26.196
We can never go back to the source,

00:07:26.196 --> 00:07:28.881
and the source is God,
with our bucket full

00:07:28.881 --> 00:07:30.861
and get replenished and get a new mind set

00:07:30.861 --> 00:07:33.747
and get a new spirit
and get fresh anointing.

00:07:33.747 --> 00:07:36.385
When I empty my bucket every day,

00:07:36.385 --> 00:07:38.357
I know the next day when I wake up,

00:07:38.357 --> 00:07:39.592
my bucket will be back full.

00:07:39.592 --> 00:07:42.247
But the way I empty my bucket
is if I can empty my bucket

00:07:42.247 --> 00:07:44.527
and give everything I got
and it gives you life.

00:07:44.527 --> 00:07:46.922
If I can empty my bucket
and give everything I got

00:07:46.922 --> 00:07:48.347
and put some fire in your life.

00:07:48.347 --> 00:07:50.737
If I can empty my bucket
and give everything I got

00:07:50.737 --> 00:07:51.746
and it inspires you.

00:07:51.746 --> 00:07:53.775
If I can empty my bucket
and give everything I got

00:07:53.775 --> 00:07:55.157
and it empowers you,

00:07:55.157 --> 00:07:58.290
my job is done with the
way that I live my life.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:07:59.755
But the thing you have to understand,

00:07:59.755 --> 00:08:03.882
in order to live a full life,
you have to empty your bucket.

00:08:03.882 --> 00:08:05.410
But the thing I can guarantee you

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:06.908
about emptying your bucket,

00:08:06.908 --> 00:08:08.736
your family's life will be made richer,

00:08:08.736 --> 00:08:10.293
your workplace will be made richer

00:08:10.293 --> 00:08:13.089
and you as a person, when you
look in the mirror at night,

00:08:13.089 --> 00:08:15.222
you will have this fulfillment,
you will have this joy,

00:08:15.222 --> 00:08:17.363
and you will have this
peace that comes over you

00:08:17.363 --> 00:08:20.808
and you will say, "Man, I
gave everything I had today.

00:08:20.808 --> 00:08:22.112
"It wasn't about my circumstance.

00:08:22.112 --> 00:08:23.670
"It wasn't about my position.

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:25.098
"It wasn't about pleasing my boss.

00:08:25.098 --> 00:08:27.468
"It was about me taking pride in what I do

00:08:27.468 --> 00:08:30.168
"and the person that I am
and giving everything I got

00:08:30.168 --> 00:08:31.812
"to everything I'm involved in."

00:08:31.812 --> 00:08:32.986
Can I be honest with you?

00:08:32.986 --> 00:08:34.977
They cut me six times down my left side.

00:08:34.977 --> 00:08:36.420
One time across the left side of my neck,

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:37.999
one time across the right side of my neck,

00:08:37.999 --> 00:08:39.257
twice through my right ribs,

00:08:39.257 --> 00:08:41.264
cut out my right peck, bottom of my armpit

00:08:41.264 --> 00:08:44.454
to the bottom of my hand,
350 staples in my body

00:08:44.454 --> 00:08:48.073
and the bandaged me from
my neck to my knees.

00:08:48.073 --> 00:08:50.771
This is not lip service.

00:08:50.771 --> 00:08:51.847
I got to be honest with you.

00:08:51.847 --> 00:08:55.520
There was days to where
if I could've laid there,

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:57.902
I would've laid there.

00:08:57.902 --> 00:09:01.485
But my spirit said,
"It's not who you are."

00:09:03.258 --> 00:09:06.758
My mentality said, "It's not who you are."

00:09:07.784 --> 00:09:11.112
I don't know about you all,
but I'm a fighter, man.

00:09:11.112 --> 00:09:12.861
I fight for my goals.

00:09:12.861 --> 00:09:14.670
I fight for my dreams.

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:16.373
I fight for the things that I represent

00:09:16.373 --> 00:09:18.329
and the things I'm a part of.

00:09:18.329 --> 00:09:22.046
I dare you, the things that you do,

00:09:22.046 --> 00:09:23.076
the things that you're a part of

00:09:23.076 --> 00:09:24.827
and the things that you're connected to,

00:09:24.827 --> 00:09:26.371
I dare you every single day to show up

00:09:26.371 --> 00:09:28.529
and give everything you got.

00:09:28.529 --> 00:09:30.248
I dare you every single
day when you wake up

00:09:30.248 --> 00:09:32.072
you understand you represent something

00:09:32.072 --> 00:09:33.175
a lot greater than yourself.

00:09:33.175 --> 00:09:35.196
I dare you to go with 15 represented,

00:09:35.196 --> 00:09:36.142
give everything you got.

00:09:36.142 --> 00:09:38.222
Go home to your family,
go to your careers,

00:09:38.222 --> 00:09:40.429
give everything you got to
every aspect of your life

00:09:40.429 --> 00:09:42.417
and I dare you to watch what happens.

00:09:42.417 --> 00:09:44.596
As a matter of fact, like my
five-year-old son tells me,

00:09:44.596 --> 00:09:45.936
"I double dog dare you."

00:09:45.936 --> 00:09:48.577
(audience laughs)

00:09:48.577 --> 00:09:50.774
I don't believe in excuses.

00:09:50.774 --> 00:09:51.613
Because the thing about it,

00:09:51.613 --> 00:09:52.735
when you make an excuse,

00:09:52.735 --> 00:09:54.335
the thing you have to realize about life,

00:09:54.335 --> 00:09:56.358
somebody has it 10 times worse than you.

00:09:56.358 --> 00:09:58.647
And you make an excuse
because your soft, man.

00:09:58.647 --> 00:10:01.647
(audience applauds)

00:10:04.233 --> 00:10:05.559
I never cheated myself.

00:10:05.559 --> 00:10:06.926
Ever since I was seven years old

00:10:06.926 --> 00:10:08.025
and everything that I did,

00:10:08.025 --> 00:10:09.697
I took pride in what I did.

00:10:09.697 --> 00:10:11.550
I firmly believe the harder you work,

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:13.363
the harder it is to surrender.

00:10:13.363 --> 00:10:14.922
You see, a lot of people understand,

00:10:14.922 --> 00:10:16.691
if you go through life
and you cheat yourself

00:10:16.691 --> 00:10:17.707
there is going to come a time

00:10:17.707 --> 00:10:19.309
when you meet a certain piece of adversity

00:10:19.309 --> 00:10:21.209
and if you're not who
you're supposed to be,

00:10:21.209 --> 00:10:24.486
adversity will always introduce
you into who you really are.

00:10:24.486 --> 00:10:25.649
If you haven't been working hard

00:10:25.649 --> 00:10:27.040
and you haven't been sacrificing

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:28.732
and you haven't been emptying that bucket

00:10:28.732 --> 00:10:30.116
and you haven't been going all in

00:10:30.116 --> 00:10:32.825
in every aspect of your life,
it's going to crush you.

00:10:32.825 --> 00:10:34.572
It's going to make you give up.

00:10:34.572 --> 00:10:35.590
It's going to make you stop.

00:10:35.590 --> 00:10:37.086
It's going to make you make excuses.

00:10:37.086 --> 00:10:40.565
But if you work hard, if you
got a certain person in you

00:10:40.565 --> 00:10:42.927
that when you at adversity
and you at opposition

00:10:42.927 --> 00:10:44.296
and you want to make excuses,

00:10:44.296 --> 00:10:45.470
then that person inside you says,

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:47.362
"Man, you ain't built like that.

00:10:47.362 --> 00:10:49.370
"You know you better than that.

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:51.747
"You know you're not like that, man."

00:10:51.747 --> 00:10:55.131
You deal with it and keep
going and you embrace it, man.

00:10:55.131 --> 00:10:56.231
That's what life's about.

00:10:56.231 --> 00:10:57.950
That's how people get stronger.

00:10:57.950 --> 00:11:00.328
People don't get stronger
by you making excuses.

00:11:00.328 --> 00:11:02.553
People get stronger by when
you go through adversity

00:11:02.553 --> 00:11:04.039
and you go through
trials and tribulations.

00:11:04.039 --> 00:11:05.565
You look at it and when
it hits you in the face,

00:11:05.565 --> 00:11:06.772
you back up a little bit,

00:11:06.772 --> 00:11:08.402
and it hits you again,
you back up a little bit

00:11:08.402 --> 00:11:09.426
and you stand back up and you say,

00:11:09.426 --> 00:11:11.746
"If that's all you got, you in trouble."

00:11:11.746 --> 00:11:13.743
When you think about life,
everybody wants the prize

00:11:13.743 --> 00:11:15.613
but nobody wants the process.

00:11:15.613 --> 00:11:16.747
Everybody wants the championship

00:11:16.747 --> 00:11:18.418
but nobody wants the day-to-day.

00:11:18.418 --> 00:11:19.641
Everybody wants to win games

00:11:19.641 --> 00:11:20.767
but nobody wants to put in the work

00:11:20.767 --> 00:11:22.483
that it takes to win games.

00:11:22.483 --> 00:11:24.545
In the Bible, it talks
about in Proverbs, it says,

00:11:24.545 --> 00:11:27.226
"The laborer's appetite works for him

00:11:27.226 --> 00:11:29.173
"and his hunger drives him on."

00:11:29.173 --> 00:11:31.727
"The laborer's appetite works for him

00:11:31.727 --> 00:11:33.456
"and his hunger drives him on."

00:11:33.456 --> 00:11:35.075
So, my question to you all is,

00:11:35.075 --> 00:11:37.004
what's your appetite for winning?

00:11:37.004 --> 00:11:38.691
Because if you have an
appetite for winning,

00:11:38.691 --> 00:11:40.365
your hunger will drive you every day.

00:11:40.365 --> 00:11:42.136
Your hunger will take
you to the weight room.

00:11:42.136 --> 00:11:43.737
Your hunger will take you past 32.

00:11:43.737 --> 00:11:45.618
Your hunger will take
you past the opposition.

00:11:45.618 --> 00:11:47.275
Your hunger will take you past adversity.

00:11:47.275 --> 00:11:49.679
Your hunger will take you past
the trials and tribulation.

00:11:49.679 --> 00:11:51.171
Your hunger will take you
to that fourth quarter

00:11:51.171 --> 00:11:52.655
when there's four zeroes on that clock,

00:11:52.655 --> 00:11:53.563
you have emptied that bucket,

00:11:53.563 --> 00:11:55.767
you have given everything
you had in that game.

00:11:55.767 --> 00:11:56.985
See, it's that sort of mind set, man,

00:11:56.985 --> 00:11:57.960
where you attack this thing.

00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:00.469
The game of football,
it's not about skill.

00:12:00.469 --> 00:12:02.724
That what people miss the boat on.

00:12:02.724 --> 00:12:03.862
It has nothing to do with skill.

00:12:03.862 --> 00:12:05.689
It has nothing to do with a 40 yard dash.

00:12:05.689 --> 00:12:07.973
It has nothing to do with
jumping a 40 inch vertical.

00:12:07.973 --> 00:12:10.267
What this game is about, it's about will,

00:12:10.267 --> 00:12:11.563
that's it.

00:12:11.563 --> 00:12:13.682
It's not about skill,
this game is about will.

00:12:13.682 --> 00:12:15.112
So, the moment that you
make up in your mind

00:12:15.112 --> 00:12:16.919
the day that you make up in your mind

00:12:16.919 --> 00:12:18.315
that you are going to
play this game for God

00:12:18.315 --> 00:12:19.646
and give everything you got to it,

00:12:19.646 --> 00:12:21.716
you can't help but to
give everything you got.

00:12:21.716 --> 00:12:23.246
That's the moment that you will realize

00:12:23.246 --> 00:12:24.997
this game has nothing to do with skill.

00:12:24.997 --> 00:12:27.349
I've seen plenty of talented guys fold.

00:12:27.349 --> 00:12:29.354
I've seen plenty of talented
guys get hit in the mouth

00:12:29.354 --> 00:12:30.187
and they didn't want it.

00:12:30.187 --> 00:12:31.458
I've seen plenty of talented guys

00:12:31.458 --> 00:12:33.390
get punched in the face and
they go back to the sideline

00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:34.497
and they stand beside their coach

00:12:34.497 --> 00:12:35.672
and they don't want it no more.

00:12:35.672 --> 00:12:36.600
They make up excuses.

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:37.919
I've seen plenty of talented guys,

00:12:37.919 --> 00:12:40.842
they ran a 4.2 in a 40,
they bench press 325 pounds,

00:12:40.842 --> 00:12:42.605
and when third and one came
up they tapped their helmet

00:12:42.605 --> 00:12:43.872
to come out of the game.

00:12:43.872 --> 00:12:46.705
That has nothing to do with skill.

00:12:47.623 --> 00:12:48.743
But I thought I was all in

00:12:48.743 --> 00:12:50.165
and I thought I was giving
it everything I had.

00:12:50.165 --> 00:12:50.998
My father would say to me,

00:12:50.998 --> 00:12:52.633
"Son, I need you to empty your bucket.

00:12:52.633 --> 00:12:54.059
"Son, I need you to
give everything you got.

00:12:54.059 --> 00:12:55.479
"Son, no matter how hard you work,

00:12:55.479 --> 00:12:56.387
"there was somebody beside you

00:12:56.387 --> 00:12:57.670
"that works even harder than you."

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:59.491
He would say to me, "Son,
what brings you here?

00:12:59.491 --> 00:13:00.419
"You have two more years

00:13:00.419 --> 00:13:02.208
"that you haven't even tapped into yet.

00:13:02.208 --> 00:13:03.675
"You haven't even pushed
yourself to the limit.

00:13:03.675 --> 00:13:05.195
"You haven't even pushed
yourself to the point

00:13:05.195 --> 00:13:07.260
"to where you feel that
you can't go anymore.

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:08.411
"You have to dig a little bit deeper

00:13:08.411 --> 00:13:09.892
"and you have to push
yourself a little bit further

00:13:09.892 --> 00:13:11.353
"and you have to go a little bit harder.

00:13:11.353 --> 00:13:13.794
"You haven't even reached that point yet,

00:13:13.794 --> 00:13:15.540
"If you can push yourself to that point

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:17.245
"to where you have to
dig a little bit deeper,

00:13:17.245 --> 00:13:18.923
"to where you feel as if
you're about to pass out,

00:13:18.923 --> 00:13:20.152
"you're working so hard,

00:13:20.152 --> 00:13:23.319
"that's when you come and talk to me."

00:13:24.386 --> 00:13:26.020
If your life doesn't have purpose

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:29.629
and life is like a pencil with no end.

00:13:29.629 --> 00:13:30.962
It has no point.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:35.785
Every day you get up, you
don't have any direction.

00:13:35.785 --> 00:13:38.671
But when you get up every
day and you have a purpose,

00:13:38.671 --> 00:13:40.180
you have a paralyzed right arm and hand

00:13:40.180 --> 00:13:42.668
and they say, "Hey, man, you
can't use that arm anymore."

00:13:42.668 --> 00:13:45.695
I say, "I'm using this arm every day

00:13:45.695 --> 00:13:47.923
"by the way that I live my life."

00:13:47.923 --> 00:13:49.954
Because my life has purpose.

00:13:49.954 --> 00:13:51.631
I don't live my life for me.

00:13:51.631 --> 00:13:53.338
That's why some of the decisions
and some of the choices

00:13:53.338 --> 00:13:56.176
that I had to make, nobody understood.

00:13:56.176 --> 00:13:58.437
Because it wasn't about Inky Johnson,

00:13:58.437 --> 00:14:00.237
it was about those that
paved the way for me.

00:14:00.237 --> 00:14:01.299
I was honoring them.

00:14:01.299 --> 00:14:03.667
And about the ones that
were coming behind me,

00:14:03.667 --> 00:14:05.835
I had to leave a legacy for them.

00:14:05.835 --> 00:14:09.281
Every day you wake up, make
it bigger than just your job.

00:14:09.281 --> 00:14:10.447
That's how you become a champion.

00:14:10.447 --> 00:14:11.801
That's how you really all live.

00:14:11.801 --> 00:14:13.183
That's how you empty your bucket.

00:14:13.183 --> 00:14:14.344
You can't just empty your bucket

00:14:14.344 --> 00:14:15.492
and call yourself a champion.

00:14:15.492 --> 00:14:17.024
If you just come into an office

00:14:17.024 --> 00:14:18.667
or you just do your job
and you do it great.

00:14:18.667 --> 00:14:21.024
You do a great job, but
you're a public success

00:14:21.024 --> 00:14:23.441
but you're a private failure.

00:14:25.744 --> 00:14:28.897
You're a public success but
you're a private failure.

00:14:28.897 --> 00:14:32.344
You don't give everything
you got to your family.

00:14:32.344 --> 00:14:35.257
You don't give everything you got to God.

00:14:35.257 --> 00:14:38.020
You see, when I speak, I'm not
talking about just football.

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:39.891
When I speak, I'm just not
talking about your job.

00:14:39.891 --> 00:14:42.077
I'm talking about taking
every aspect of your life

00:14:42.077 --> 00:14:43.049
to the next level.

00:14:43.049 --> 00:14:44.510
That's what emptying the bucket is.

00:14:44.510 --> 00:14:46.625
See, when I step on the stage
and I give everything I got,

00:14:46.625 --> 00:14:48.757
when I get home tonight, I
don't care what time it is,

00:14:48.757 --> 00:14:50.734
I'm going to wake my wife up,
I'm going to wake my kids up

00:14:50.734 --> 00:14:51.612
and you know what I'm going to do?

00:14:51.612 --> 00:14:54.480
I'm going to get on my knees
and I'm going to pray there.

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:56.238
(audience applauds)

00:14:56.238 --> 00:14:57.440
Doctor walked by my bed, he said,

00:14:57.440 --> 00:14:59.657
"Ink, we'll get to know each other well,

00:14:59.657 --> 00:15:01.189
"you'll be in this hospital
for the next 40 days."

00:15:01.189 --> 00:15:05.106
I walked out of that
hospital on the third day.

00:15:06.190 --> 00:15:09.023
I was back in class the next week.

00:15:10.375 --> 00:15:12.520
I was back at practice in the
sand pit with my teammates

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:13.687
the next week.

00:15:16.826 --> 00:15:19.264
I had to learn how to
write all over again.

00:15:19.264 --> 00:15:21.747
I had to learn how to walk all over again.

00:15:21.747 --> 00:15:22.726
People come up to me all the time,

00:15:22.726 --> 00:15:24.124
"Ink, how did you do it, man?"

00:15:24.124 --> 00:15:26.421
"How did you make it out
of the hospital, man?"

00:15:26.421 --> 00:15:27.254
"How did you do it?"

00:15:27.254 --> 00:15:28.942
It's cute to them, right?

00:15:28.942 --> 00:15:32.238
It's cute, it's cute to them, right?

00:15:32.238 --> 00:15:34.294
"How did you do it, man?"

00:15:34.294 --> 00:15:35.604
And people don't understand when I say

00:15:35.604 --> 00:15:36.861
the process saved my life.

00:15:36.861 --> 00:15:38.445
They don't get it.

00:15:38.445 --> 00:15:39.990
When I say the process saved my life

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:41.960
and the process is more
important than the product,

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:43.254
what I'm trying to tell 'em was,

00:15:43.254 --> 00:15:45.364
when I was in park with my
mother when I was seven years old

00:15:45.364 --> 00:15:46.525
and she was sittin' in a Buick Regal,

00:15:46.525 --> 00:15:48.222
that saved my life.

00:15:48.222 --> 00:15:50.289
When I was up every Saturday
at 4 o'clock in the morning

00:15:50.289 --> 00:15:51.711
running two miles to a fire station,

00:15:51.711 --> 00:15:53.528
two miles back home, that saved my life.

00:15:53.528 --> 00:15:55.297
When I never cheated, that saved my life.

00:15:55.297 --> 00:15:57.300
When I didn't let my
teammates give up and quit,

00:15:57.300 --> 00:15:58.977
that saved my life.

00:15:58.977 --> 00:16:01.068
Because my arm and my hand was paralyzed,

00:16:01.068 --> 00:16:05.038
my spirit wasn't, my heart
wasn't, my mentality wasn't.

00:16:05.038 --> 00:16:06.026
I was the same man.

00:16:06.026 --> 00:16:07.727
I just had a paralyzed right arm and hand.

00:16:07.727 --> 00:16:10.126
It couldn't stop me if it wanted to.

00:16:10.126 --> 00:16:12.150
I couldn't quit even if I wanted to

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:13.750
because of the spirit and the soul

00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:16.254
that resided in Inky Johnson.

00:16:16.254 --> 00:16:18.409
The game created that.

00:16:18.409 --> 00:16:20.781
The process created that.

00:16:20.781 --> 00:16:22.778
So, understand, when
you're playing sports,

00:16:22.778 --> 00:16:25.902
it's a blessing because you're
in a controlled setting.

00:16:25.902 --> 00:16:28.005
It allows you to build your character.

00:16:28.005 --> 00:16:29.540
You have a bad practice,
come back tomorrow,

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:32.081
have a good practice
and make it up, buddy.

00:16:32.081 --> 00:16:33.789
Have a bad day, come back the next week,

00:16:33.789 --> 00:16:36.173
have a good day and make it up, buddy.

00:16:36.173 --> 00:16:38.913
It allows you to build your character.

00:16:38.913 --> 00:16:42.008
So, one day when you face
real life opposition,

00:16:42.008 --> 00:16:43.251
you can reveal your character

00:16:43.251 --> 00:16:45.681
and what you're really made out of.

00:16:45.681 --> 00:16:47.745
Process is more important
than the product.

00:16:47.745 --> 00:16:48.872
ESPN called me.

00:16:48.872 --> 00:16:50.689
They did a story on me this past summer.

00:16:50.689 --> 00:16:52.046
But they call me one day.

00:16:52.046 --> 00:16:53.136
I picked up the phone they said,

00:16:53.136 --> 00:16:54.491
"Is this Inky Johnson?"

00:16:54.491 --> 00:16:56.818
I said, "Last time I
checked, I'm Inky Johnson."

00:16:56.818 --> 00:16:58.732
(audience laughs)

00:16:58.732 --> 00:17:01.119
They said, "Is this this the same guy

00:17:01.119 --> 00:17:03.156
"that said if you could
change what happened to you,

00:17:03.156 --> 00:17:04.406
"you wouldn't?"

00:17:05.307 --> 00:17:07.159
I said, "Absolutely."

00:17:07.159 --> 00:17:09.260
They said, "It's our
understanding the game of football

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:10.732
"meant the world to you."

00:17:10.732 --> 00:17:12.797
I said, "At one point, it did."

00:17:12.797 --> 00:17:14.492
They said, "It's our
understanding that your family

00:17:14.492 --> 00:17:16.603
"was banking on you making it to the NFL

00:17:16.603 --> 00:17:17.624
"so they can have a better way of life."

00:17:17.624 --> 00:17:19.420
I said, "Yup, that's correct."

00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:20.434
They said, "We're coming to see you."

00:17:20.434 --> 00:17:22.077
I said, "All right, cool, come on."

00:17:22.077 --> 00:17:23.485
They said, "But we don't
want to see you in Atlanta.

00:17:23.485 --> 00:17:25.280
"We want to see you in Neyland Stadium

00:17:25.280 --> 00:17:28.000
"on the exact yard line
where your life changed,

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:29.302
"the same time of day.

00:17:29.302 --> 00:17:32.753
"The only thing that won't be
present is Air Force's team."

00:17:32.753 --> 00:17:34.213
"All right, cool."

00:17:34.213 --> 00:17:35.722
So, they take me to Neyland Stadium,

00:17:35.722 --> 00:17:38.375
they put me on the exact yard
line when my life changed.

00:17:38.375 --> 00:17:39.846
They said, "Now, tell your younger self

00:17:39.846 --> 00:17:42.442
"why you wouldn't stop
that injury if you could.

00:17:42.442 --> 00:17:43.759
"If you could be in the NFL right now

00:17:43.759 --> 00:17:45.098
"making millions of dollars,

00:17:45.098 --> 00:17:46.733
"tell your younger self
why you wouldn't change

00:17:46.733 --> 00:17:49.957
"that situation if you could."

00:17:49.957 --> 00:17:51.921
I said, "The reason I wouldn't change it,

00:17:51.921 --> 00:17:54.670
"believe or not, it has
nothing to do with me."

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:57.218
On a personal level he
thought I was going to say,

00:17:57.218 --> 00:17:58.939
"Because of the man that I've become,

00:17:58.939 --> 00:18:00.945
"the perspective that I've acquired,

00:18:00.945 --> 00:18:02.447
"my faith has been fortified."

00:18:02.447 --> 00:18:04.163
He thought I was going to
say something like that.

00:18:04.163 --> 00:18:05.608
I said, "No, it has nothing to do with me.

00:18:05.608 --> 00:18:07.388
"It has everything to do with the lives

00:18:07.388 --> 00:18:09.965
"that have been affected by
the result of the process

00:18:09.965 --> 00:18:11.842
"and the thing that I
represent in the world,

00:18:11.842 --> 00:18:13.213
"what my spirit represents."

00:18:13.213 --> 00:18:16.006
When somebody see me,
they think perseverance.

00:18:16.006 --> 00:18:17.834
What my spirit represents
when somebody see me,

00:18:17.834 --> 00:18:19.260
they think, "Don't quit."

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:21.280
